       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. No standard indication or titration schedule for amlodipine goes above 10 mg per day. A single 50 mg dose is in the range where overdose toxicity is reported. Your reply didn't name a specific condition or protocol that would justify it, so I can't treat it as an established regimen.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Dose up to 10 mg:** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily right now. If you need more blood pressure control, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide diuretic.\n- **Unusual protocol:** If this is part of a specialist or research protocol, please involve pharmacy and the attending or consulting specialist. Once they've verified it, the order can be entered with the protocol documented.\n- **Possible error:** If the number came from a transcription or unit mistake, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it.\n\nI can also enter the order with a note that asks for pharmacist review, but only at a dose within the labeled range."
      }
